=2 Walkthrough
* **{c=red:Note:}** If you did not already do so, speak with {p:Cid} (in {p:Bastok} - {z:Metalworks} - Home Point #1) to begin this Mission.
* Head to {z:Southern San d'Oria} (A-6) (Home Point #4) and speak with {n:Hinaree} on the second floor of the manor for a short cutscene.

=4 Entanglement
* Zone into {z:Port San d'Oria} for a cutscene. Using the Home Point works.
* Speak with {n:Chasalvige} (L-6) in the **Cathedral's Manuscript Room** in {z:Northern San d'Oria}, left of the entrance.

=4 Head Wind
* Travel to {z:Windurst Waters} (J-8) (Home Point #3) and speak with {n:Kerutoto} in the North wing of the {p:Rhinostery}. You may need speak with her more than once, as she offers other quests.

:* The correct cutscene for this Mission is about you "standing there like a muddled mandragora" and of a girl with "crikey-spiky hair".

* Go to {z:Windurst Walls} (E-5) (Home Point #1) and speak with {p:Yoran-Oran}.
* Head to {z:Attohwa Chasm} (H-6), enter {z:Boneyard Gully}, and prepare for a boss fight.
** {p:Home Point} #1 in {z:Attohwa Chasm} or the {p:Unity Warp} (Level 125) will get you close to the entrance.

__With the lifting of the level cap on this battlefield, this battle is now relatively trivial in difficulty. The walkthrough below was written for a level cap of 50.__
!Attohwa Chasm-map.jpg|right|Attohwa Chasm
[Useful Items to bring:
* Some form of {p:Reraise|Category:Reraise}
* Food. MP and HP regen drinks
* Any other HP or MP potions
* {@i:Blackened Siredon|5266} {i:Blackened Siredon|Blackened Siredon|5266} (its usefulness is debatable)
** __Note: __{@i:Blackened Siredon|5266}__ {i:Blackened Siredon|Blackened Siredon|5266} is an item that is used to stop the Mithran Trackers TP gain for a short amount of time.__
*** If you wish to obtain these items, you need to complete the quest {q:Mithran Delicacies|Mithran Delicacies|Mithran Delicacies} given by {n:Anguenet} at (J-10) in {z:Carpenters' Landing}. This quest is entirely optional.

]
\**{c=red:Note:}** FastCS might get you stuck in the cutscene that plays when entering. Simply unloading the addon will fix it. Similarly, if you normally play with FrameRateDivisor 1, typing //config FrameRateDivisor 2 should advance the cutscene. You may immediately re-enable 60 FPS after passing that particular line of dialogue.
* After your party is geared up and ready, click on the Dark Miasma and enter the battlefield "{M:Head Wind|Head Wind|Where Messengers Gather}". Buffs will wear off when you enter, so buff inside the battlefield.
** Read the battlefield names carefully; it is NOT the battlefield for "{p:Like the Wind}" if you happen to have that unlocked.

[Boss Name
{n:Shikaree X} (BST/NIN, assisted by {m:Shikaree X's Rabbit}){br}{m:Shikaree Y} (DRK/MNK){br}{p:Shikaree Z} (DRG/WHM, assisted by {m:Shikaree Z's Wyvern})
>Abilities
:* They can each use their job specific abilities, spells, and more importantly Weaponskills with their respective weapons.
:* They also tend to use {p:skillchains|Skillchain} and will team up accordingly.

>Notes
:* All the monsters in the battle have relatively low HP so they can be taken out fairly quickly with decent damage.
:* The problem is their high TP gain and the ability to unleash devastating weaponskills.
:* A well timed {p:Sleepga} at the start should allow everyone to take out one or more of the Mithran Trackers before the others awaken.
:* Kill the pet's master before their corresponding pet, or they will summon another.
:* {m:Shikaree Y} also {p:Counters|Counter}, so melees should attack her from the sides and back.
:* {n:Shikaree X} and {p:Shikaree Z} have {p:Utsusemi} and {s:Blink} respectively.

